  "finding": "The same native database-is-locked exception at PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL reproduces with both independently built Core 2.4.2 and current Core 2.5.0. Every initialized-file control passes. This failure class is therefore not unique to the new Core source in this toolchain/SQLite environment.",
  "timing_interpretation": "Median failing opens range from 239.5 to 498 microseconds; observed maxima reach 2,413 microseconds. These are far below the configured 2,000/30,000 ms statement budgets. These runs are diagnostic observations, not performance guarantees or a failure-rate comparison.",
  "primary_reference": {
    "url": "https://www.sqlite.org/c3ref/busy_handler.html",
    "title": "Register A Callback To Handle SQLITE_BUSY Errors",
    "paraphrase": "SQLite may omit a configured busy callback when invoking it could cause deadlock, returning SQLITE_BUSY directly. A busy timeout alone does not guarantee every lock conflict waits for that interval.",
    "scope": "Documents why immediate SQLITE_BUSY is possible; does not prove the exact internal SQLite lock state in these runs.",
